{"vid":"DR-aseNKM4A","source":"DR-aseNKM4A.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"Are you embarrassed about your pronunciation?"},{"t":3.2,"txt":"Are you worried you sound a bit robotic?"},{"t":7.2,"txt":"Don't worry."},{"t":8.1,"txt":"In this lesson, we're going to practice shadowing:"},{"t":11.4,"txt":"a powerful way to improve your fluency, pronunciation, and listening."},{"t":18.8,"txt":"You'll do this by listening to a short story about how I got trapped in a lift,"},{"t":25.6,"txt":"and how I escaped again."},{"t":28.5,"txt":"This is a shadowing lesson, which means you'll listen carefully"},{"t":33.4,"txt":"and repeat what I say, almost at the same time."},{"t":37.6,"txt":"Like an echo."},{"t":40.4,"txt":"Here's how."},{"t":41.5,"txt":"It was my first day at work and I was the last one to finish."},{"t":47,"txt":"Click here to find out more about shadowing"},{"t":50.8,"txt":"and why it's useful for your speaking, listening, and pronunciation."},{"t":55.2,"txt":"Right. Let's start the story."},{"t":61.2,"txt":"It was my first day at work, and I was the last one to finish."},{"t":66.4,"txt":"I'd just got in the lift when I noticed there weren't any buttons."},{"t":72.9,"txt":"Before I could react,"},{"t":74.4,"txt":"the doors slammed shut."},{"t":77.5,"txt":"I desperately tried to open them again, but they wouldn't budge."},{"t":82.9,"txt":"Let's have a look at the pronunciation in more detail."},{"t":86.6,"txt":"First day at work."},{"t":88.2,"txt":"Can you hear a sound at the end of 'first' in this phrase?"},{"t":92.9,"txt":"Listen again."},{"t":94.4,"txt":"First day at work."},{"t":98.6,"txt":"There isn't one."},{"t":100,"txt":"Look at the letters on either side of that 't'."},{"t":103.3,"txt":"We have an 's' and a 'd', which are pronounced /s/ and /d/."},{"t":108.8,"txt":"These are both consonant sounds."},{"t":111.5,"txt":"When a 't' is between two consonant sounds, we don't pronounce it."},{"t":117.1,"txt":"Let's call this a 'consonant sandwich'."},{"t":120.5,"txt":"We have consonant sandwiches in other phrases too."},{"t":124,"txt":"Repeat after me."},{"t":126.2,"txt":"First day at work."},{"t":132.4,"txt":"I'd just got in the lift."},{"t":139.4,"txt":"Wouldn't budge."},{"t":145.9,"txt":"Last one."},{"t":151.8,"txt":"Let's continue with the story."},{"t":154.5,"txt":"After a while, the lights began to dim."},{"t":159.3,"txt":"I desperately banged on the doors, but there was no one around."},{"t":164.9,"txt":"A few hours had passed and it was almost ten o'clock."},{"t":169.4,"txt":"I was at a complete loss."},{"t":172.1,"txt":"I've highlighted the 't' in 'it' and 'at' in these phrases."},{"t":176.9,"txt":"Listen carefully."},{"t":178.3,"txt":"What sound can you hear?"},{"t":180.5,"txt":"It was almost ten o'clock."},{"t":183.2,"txt":"I was at a complete loss."},{"t":185.8,"txt":"Instead of a /t/ sound, it's a glottal stop, which is the sound you can hear in the middle of this phrase."},{"t":195,"txt":"Uh-oh!"},{"t":197.5,"txt":"We make it by suddenly blocking the air in our throat and then releasing it."},{"t":203.5,"txt":"So instead of 'it', I make the vowel sound /ɪ/, but I cut it short in my throat."},{"t":210.5,"txt":"/ɪ/. This is very common with short words that end with 't'."},{"t":215.8,"txt":"We also have another example with 'at'."},{"t":219.2,"txt":"These sound very similar, so let's practice them both. /ɪ/. /ɪ/. /æ/. /æ/."},{"t":227.4,"txt":"Got that?"},{"t":229.3,"txt":"Let's finish the story."},{"t":231.5,"txt":"\"Why won't you open?\" I shouted in despair."},{"t":235.9,"txt":"\"Opening doors\", replied a robotic-sounding voice."},{"t":240.3,"txt":"The doors wooshed open."},{"t":242.8,"txt":"I grabbed my things and ran out as fast as I could."},{"t":247.4,"txt":"As I glanced behind me, a sign above the doors caught my eye."},{"t":251.6,"txt":"It read: \"voice-activated lift\"."},{"t":255.6,"txt":"Listen again to the 'e-d' endings in these words."},{"t":259.1,"txt":"Is the pronunciation the same, or different?"},{"t":263.2,"txt":"Shouted. Wooshed. Grabbed."},{"t":269.8,"txt":"We have three different ways to pronounce 'e-d'."},{"t":274.8,"txt":"/ɪd/."},{"t":276.6,"txt":"/t/."},{"t":278.6,"txt":"/d/."},{"t":280.6,"txt":"Let's start with 'shouted'."},{"t":282.6,"txt":"When a verb ends with a 'd' or a 't' like 'shout' or 'need',"},{"t":287.9,"txt":"the '-ed' ending is pronounced as /ɪd/."},{"t":291,"txt":"So we say: 'shouted', 'started', 'needed'."},{"t":298.5,"txt":"Those last two weren't in the story: they were just examples."},{"t":302.7,"txt":"But how about 'wooshed'?"},{"t":305,"txt":"If a verb ends with an unvoiced consonant sound,"},{"t":308.8,"txt":"meaning you can't feel a vibration in your throat, so sounds like /ʃ/ or /s/"},{"t":316.7,"txt":"We pronounce the 'ed' ending as a /t/, so we say 'wooshed', 'glanced', passed'."},{"t":328,"txt":"And lastly we have 'grabbed'."},{"t":332,"txt":"If a verb ends with a voiced consonant,"},{"t":335,"txt":"meaning we can feel a vibration in our throat when we say it, like /b/"},{"t":340.7,"txt":"and /ŋ/, the '-ed' is pronounced as /d/."},{"t":345.6,"txt":"This also applies to vowel sounds like the /aɪ/ in 'reply'."},{"t":351.3,"txt":"Repeat after me."},{"t":353.1,"txt":"Replied. Grabbed. Banged."},{"t":360.2,"txt":"With all of that in mind,"},{"t":362.1,"txt":"It's time to shadow the entire story again."},{"t":366.2,"txt":"Let's see if you can improve your pronunciation."},{"t":372.8,"txt":"It was my first day at work and I was the last one to finish."},{"t":378.1,"txt":"I'd just got in the lift when I noticed there weren't any buttons."},{"t":384.6,"txt":"Before I could react,"},{"t":386.1,"txt":"the doors slammed shut."},{"t":389.1,"txt":"I desperately tried to open them again, but they wouldn't budge."},{"t":395,"txt":"After a while, the lights began to dim."},{"t":399.8,"txt":"I desperately banged on the doors, but there was no one around."},{"t":405.4,"txt":"A few hours had passed and it was almost ten o'clock."},{"t":409.9,"txt":"I was at a complete loss."},{"t":413.1,"txt":"\"Why won't you open?\""},{"t":415.5,"txt":"I shouted in despair."},{"t":417.5,"txt":"\"Opening doors\", replied a robotic-sounding voice."},{"t":422,"txt":"The doors wooshed open."},{"t":424.5,"txt":"I grabbed my things and ran out as fast as I could."},{"t":429,"txt":"As I glanced behind me, a sign above the doors caught my eye."},{"t":433.2,"txt":"It read 'voice-activated lift'."},{"t":437,"txt":"How was that for you?"},{"t":439.1,"txt":"Was your pronunciation better the second time?"},{"t":442.1,"txt":"Remember, you can download a free audio file of this story by clicking here."},{"t":447.8,"txt":"And if you want more information on the pronunciation of '-ed' endings, click here."},{"t":453.8,"txt":"Have you ever been stuck somewhere?"},{"t":456.3,"txt":"How did you get out?"},{"t":458.1,"txt":"Let us know in the comments - and see you in the next video! Bye bye!"}],"words":[{"t":0.04,"w":"Are"},{"t":0.04,"w":"you"},{"t":0.04,"w":"embarrassed"},{"t":0.04,"w":"about"},{"t":0.04,"w":"your"},{"t":0.04,"w":"pronunciation?"},{"t":3.16,"w":"Are"},{"t":3.16,"w":"you"},{"t":3.16,"w":"worried"},{"t":3.16,"w":"you"},{"t":3.16,"w":"sound"},{"t":3.16,"w":"a"},{"t":3.16,"w":"bit"},{"t":3.16,"w":"robotic?"},{"t":7.234,"w":"Don't"},{"t":7.234,"w":"worry."},{"t":8.08,"w":"In"},{"t":8.08,"w":"this"},{"t":8.08,"w":"lesson,"},{"t":8.08,"w":"we're"},{"t":8.08,"w":"going"},{"t":8.08,"w":"to"},{"t":8.08,"w":"practice"},{"t":8.08,"w":"shadowing:"},{"t":11.4,"w":"a"},{"t":11.4,"w":"powerful"},{"t":11.4,"w":"way"},{"t":11.4,"w":"to"},{"t":11.4,"w":"improve"},{"t":11.4,"w":"your"},{"t":11.4,"w":"fluency,"},{"t":11.4,"w":"pronunciation,"},{"t":11.4,"w":"and"},{"t":11.4,"w":"listening."},{"t":18.84,"w":"You'll"},{"t":18.84,"w":"do"},{"t":18.84,"w":"this"},{"t":18.84,"w":"by"},{"t":18.84,"w":"listening"},{"t":18.84,"w":"to"},{"t":18.84,"w":"a"},{"t":18.84,"w":"short"},{"t":18.84,"w":"story"},{"t":18.84,"w":"about"},{"t":18.8